   "evidence": "Helicities are \u00b11/2, so `\u039b-\u03bb \u2208 {0, \u00b11}` and the exponent ranges over `{0, \u00b11, \u00b12}`; for `idxPM = (+1/2,-1/2)` and `idxMP = (-1/2,+1/2)` (Positivity.lean:104,107) the exponent is `1-(-1) = 2` and the phase is `+1`, not `-1`.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Particles/Parton/PDF/ComplexSpinDensity.lean",
   "fix": "Drop \"exactly\": \"...up to the phase `(-1)^{(\u039b-\u03bb)-(\u039b'-\u03bb')}`, which is `1` on these entries\" \u2014 the restriction to them comes from angular-momentum conservation, which the next sentences already say.",
   "issue": "The `IsParityInvariant` docstring says the phase `(-1)^{(\u039b-\u03bb)-(\u039b'-\u03bb')}` is `1` \"exactly on these entries\" (those with `\u039b-\u03bb = \u039b'-\u03bb'`). The phase is `1` whenever the exponent is even, which also includes the forward-forbidden entries with `(\u039b-\u03bb)-(\u039b'-\u03bb') = \u00b12`, e.g. `(idxPM, idxMP)`. As written the reader is told those entries carry a `-1`, which is wrong.",
